THE CONDITIONAL CONSEQUENCE - DECIDED HERE, NOT DEFERRED
================================================================================

  AAP 0.6.1 makes four deliverables conditional on this tool writing an artifact.
  The observed outcome is NO ARTIFACT, so the decision is:

      harness/lib/normalize/adapters/osv_scanner.py            NOT CREATED
      oss-scan-results/adapter-tests/fixtures/osv-scanner.json NOT CREATED
      oss-scan-results/adapter-tests/expected/osv-scanner.rows.json
                                                               NOT CREATED
      oss-scan-results/adapter-tests/test_osv_scanner_adapter.py
                                                               NOT CREATED

  Decided by the observed Stage 3 outcome and not left open. There is no artifact
  to route, so there is no adapter to write, no captured fixture to derive one
  from and no expected-rows file to hand-verify against. A fixture invented for a
  file the tool never wrote would be a fabricated measurement.

  Two consequences that follow and must not be lost:

  - RECONCILIATION for this tool is recorded as

        not applicable - artifact absent

    and NEVER as '0 = 0'. AAP 0.5.4 is explicit: the identity 'raw finding records
    = dataset rows + rejected records' presupposes an artifact to traverse. Zero
    equals zero would assert that a traversal happened and balanced, when no
    traversal was possible. The distinction is what keeps an absent artifact
    distinguishable from an artifact that parsed to nothing.

  - THE NINE-TOOL INVENTORY still carries osv-scanner. findings.json and
    findings.csv are row-only, so a tool with zero rows is by construction
    invisible in them. oss-scan-results/tool-status.md and
    oss-scan-results/severity-map.md are the authoritative inventory of all nine
    and each must hold an osv-scanner entry - tool-status.md with the full
    per-tool contract including the verbatim stderr and the completion verdict
    above, severity-map.md with the entry for a tool that contributed no row and
    therefore no native severity literal.

  Note that harness/lib/normalize/shape.py already declares an 'osv-scanner'
  routing key deliberately, so a legitimately written artifact would have been
  DETECTED by shape rather than falling into the unknown-shape halt. Detection is
  not routing, and the distinction matters: harness/lib/normalize/cli.py line 392
  declares CONDITIONAL_ADAPTER_MODULES = ("osv_scanner",) and lines 1133-1149
  raise MissingAdapterModule - reject class missing_adapter_module - because
  harness/lib/normalize/adapters/osv_scanner.py does not exist in this checkout,
  by the AAP 0.6.1 conditional this observed outcome decided. So the accurate
  statement is: the shape would be recognised, and normalization would then HALT
  with missing_adapter_module until the conditional adapter exists. It would not
  silently emit zero rows, and it would not route to another tool's adapter. The
  halt is the designed behaviour, not a gap - a recognised shape with no adapter
  must stop rather than be dropped - and the four conditional deliverables
  (adapter, fixture, expected rows, test module) are created together if and only
  if an artifact is written.

